v class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1337894-who-wrote-the-errata-for-the-1st-edition-core-book-aberrant?p=1337996#post1337996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To what errata are you referring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jetstream has it right. It is the Errata published in the Aberrant Player\u2019s Guide.<br /> <br /> I swear it was also published digitally before the Player\u2019s Guide was published, though your cited archived website dose not show it. Dose anyone else recall if it was released by the writers digital around that time? Perhaps it was only released in a similar format on the Forum itself.<br /> <br /> EDITED ADD-ON:<br /> <br /> Getting myself back on track, that would mean the possible scribes could be; John Chambers, Chris Haddad, Bruce Baugh, Andrew Bates, Deird're Brooks, Steve Kenson, Kraig Blackwelder, and/or Jess Heinig.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling it may be Mr. Blackwelder. Errata seems like something a Developer would like to weigh in on directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 09-26-2019, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}